  "tertiaryNote": "Added at the END of the description (after the principal soil name and other constituents) using qualitative 'with ...' terms, e.g. 'SAND with rare gravel size brick fragments'. The size of the tertiary fractions may also be given in mm. The tertiary fraction does not need to be quantified and no percentage definition is given for the qualitative terms; they relate to identifying the geological unit (e.g. less than about 10% by mass in a fine soil, or about 2% in a coarse soil). Terms must be applied consistently on any given job.",
  "plasticity": [
    {
      "term": "Non-plastic",
      "criteria": "A 3 mm thread cannot be rolled at any water content.",
      "ref": "BS 5930:2015+A1:2020 Table 23 (clause 34.3.4)"
    },
    {
      "term": "Low",
      "criteria": "The thread can barely be rolled and the lump cannot be formed when drier than the plastic limit.",
      "ref": "BS 5930:2015+A1:2020 Table 23 (clause 34.3.4)"
    },
    {
      "term": "Medium",
      "criteria": "The thread is easy to roll and not much time is required to reach the plastic limit. The thread cannot be rerolled after reaching the plastic limit. The lump crumbles when drier than the plastic limit.",
      "ref": "BS 5930:2015+A1:2020 Table 23 (clause 34.3.4)"
    },
    {
      "term": "High",
      "criteria": "It takes considerable time rolling and kneading to reach the plastic limit. The thread can be rerolled several times after reaching the plastic limit. The lump can be formed without crumbling when drier than the plastic limit.",
      "ref": "BS 5930:2015+A1:2020 Table 23 (clause 34.3.4)"
    }
  ],
